# src/shared/ipcPayloads.ts and tests/unit/ipcPayloads.test.ts each embed a raw
# control byte (a literal NUL, and in ipcPayloads.ts a literal 0x1F too) as part
# of deliberately validating/testing for control characters in untrusted input.
# Without help, git's binary-content heuristic classifies both files as binary
# and prints "Binary files ... differ" for any diff that touches them — silently
# omitting their content from code review. That is especially dangerous for
# ipcPayloads.ts, which validates every untrusted payload from the renderer and
# from target pages: a reviewer reading a generated diff has no signal that a
# change there was skipped. The `diff` attribute (not `text`) forces a textual
# diff without enabling end-of-line normalisation, so it cannot rewrite any
# file's contents on checkout — it only changes how git displays changes.
*.ts diff
*.tsx diff
